      en: 'Kalagachia eco-tourism centre lies in the western Sundarbans, reached by trawler from Nildumur ghat in Shyamnagar upazila of Satkhira across the Kholpetua River and a maze of tidal creeks. Compared with Karamjal it sees far fewer visitors, so the silence of the forest and the calls of birds come through much more clearly.\n\nThe centre has a wooden trail into the forest and a watchtower. Along the way you will almost certainly meet troops of monkeys and, with some luck, spotted deer, while the mud is busy with crabs of many kinds. The boat journey is half the pleasure: walls of golpata palm, keora and goran on both banks, and small fishing boats slipping in and out of side channels.\n\nNovember to March is ideal, with calm water, clear skies and more migratory birds. During the monsoon the rivers turn rough, making the trip less safe.',
