      en: 'The village of Pithabhog in Rupsha upazila of Khulna is traditionally regarded as the home of the Tagore family’s earliest known ancestors. According to the commonly told history, a branch of the Kushari lineage from which the Tagores descend later moved from this area towards Calcutta, eventually giving rise to the famous Tagore family of Jorasanko.\n\nThere is no grand mansion here today. Instead you will find a preserved plot marking the ancestral homestead, a memorial plaque and a few modest commemorative structures, surrounded by coconut and betel-nut groves, ponds and the quiet rhythm of village life in rural Khulna.\n\nFor admirers of Tagore, the visit is a kind of journey to the roots rather than a sightseeing stop. It takes little time on site, but the ride across the Rupsha Bridge and along country lanes is pleasant in winter, and it combines well with the Dakshindihi complex or an evening at the bridge.',
