      en: 'In the village of Ajodhya near Bagerhat stands Kodla Math, a tall brick temple tower that tapers upward like a slender pyramid. It is usually dated to the 17th century, and an inscription over the entrance is said to record that it was built in honour of a Brahmin. The tower is a protected monument under the Department of Archaeology.\n\nIts outer walls are covered with terracotta plaques of floral and geometric designs, many of them worn by centuries of weather. Rising above the flat surrounding countryside, the tower is visible from quite a distance.\n\nThe setting is completely peaceful: trees, ponds and the everyday life of the village going on around the monument. It makes a rewarding extra stop for anyone visiting the Sixty Dome Mosque and the other Bagerhat monuments, and the reddish brick glows beautifully in winter sunlight.',
