      en: 'Benapole in Sharsha upazila of Jashore is Bangladesh’s busiest land port, facing Petrapole on the Indian side. Thousands of travellers and hundreds of cargo trucks pass through every day, so the area is constantly bustling with movement.\n\nIn the late afternoon, shortly before sunset, Bangladesh’s BGB and India’s BSF hold a joint flag-lowering retreat parade at the zero line of the checkpost. The stamping of boots, synchronised marching and the moment when both flags come down together create real excitement among spectators, and seating areas are set aside for the crowd on both sides.\n\nThe parade time shifts with the season, and the ceremony may occasionally be suspended for security reasons, so check locally before making the trip. Weekends and holidays draw the largest crowds; arrive early to get a good spot.',
